      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "यथासङ्गवतो जनस्य भुवनाधिपत्यभोगाद्याः पदार्थाः भवन्तीत्यर्थः (Râmarshi.) भुवनाधिप-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "त्यं तथा भोगः विषयानुभवः (Râmarshi.) Perhaps to take it as a षष्ठीतत्पुरुष",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "would be better. कृपण comp. Bṛihadâraṇyaka Upanishad यो वा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "एतदक्षरं गार्ग्यविदित्वेतस्माल्लोकात्प्रैति स कृपणः. मत = esteemed. Comp. Nîtis'a-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "taka St. 79 and note. Compare generally Stanza 80. The Stanza",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "occurs at p. 315 of the Kâvyasangraha.—Vasantatilakâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXXVII.—मानसचापलेन = with the agility of the mind, with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the speed of thought. Râmarshi takes मानस as a vocative which",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "is, perhaps, better. As it stands, the Stanza must be taken to be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "addressed to man in general, as a very similar Stanza in the Bhâ-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "minîvilâsa IV., 11. On पाताल Râmarshi says पातालमित्युपलक्षणं तलवितल-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "सुतलतलातलमहातलरसातलपातालानीत्यर्थः अथवा पातालमित्युक्त्या नीचवस्तुषु गच्छसि.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "भ्रान्त्या = केनापि कथाप्रसङ्गेनापि (Râmarshi.). “Even by mistake” is closer",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "and appropriate too; not only do you not think of the Brahma",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "on purpose, you do not even by mistake stumble on it. आत्मनीन",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "= beneficial to oneself. Siddh. Kaum. I., 626.—Vasantatilakâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXXVIII.—निभृतप्रारब्ध = निभृतं पूर्णं यथा भवति तथा प्रारब्धाः कर्तुमिषिताः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "(Râmarshi,) steadily, unswervingly seems to be the meaning of निभृत",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "here. पुनरुक्तभुक्त = पुनरुक्तं वारंवारं भुक्ता. (Râmarshi) comp. पुनरुक्तदारुण.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "Mâlatî-Mâdhava p. 142; superfluously enjoyed i. e. enjoyed",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "over and over again. विषयाः सुखदुःखादयः says Râmarshi.—S'ârdû-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "lavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXXIX.—विरतिरेव वनिता; विरति = indifference to worldly",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "pleasures. भूति = splendour; and the ashes applied by ascetics to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "their bodies. The Stanza occurs at p. 316 of the Kâvyasangraha.—",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "S'ikharinî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. LXXX.—महाशासन = परमात्मज्ञाने स्फुरति सति (Râmarshi.) It",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "means ‘whose commands are great’; thus in one of the Upani-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "shads एतस्य वा अक्षरस्य गार्गि प्रशासने सूर्याचन्द्रमसौ तिष्ठतः or भीषास्माद्वातः पवते",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "&c.; the greatness consisting in the great powers which obey",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
